note Frost (tier II): a circle (X1 . Y1) with a seven-pointed loop (X7 . Y7) and Z2: root and SEVENTH, the interval no other aqueous spell
note has. Everything slows and freezes: the surface stretched to half speed, the droplets an octave up with a little inharmonic stretch
note (glass) gathered onto a harmonic-seventh chord, the family's only oscillator (a stretched, bright tone at C6) swelling with the orb's
note reach, the freezing splash on lock and the swish-whip as the ice cracks on unlock. The bed all but gone.

